   "source": [
    "# Phase 2-plus — Step 3: Re-evaluating Dynamic RRF at Scale\n",
    "\n",
    "## Hypothesis\n",
    "In Phase 2 Step 2, the Intent Router showed marginal improvement on the 33-chunk corpus due to four structural ceiling factors (thematic homogeneity, high top-K/corpus ratio, engine overlap, PII size asymmetry). \n",
    "\n",
    "With the augmented 228-chunk corpus (6.9x larger, 6 departments, multiple competing PII sources), we hypothesize that:\n",
    "- The **static α=0.5 baseline will degrade** because the noise pulls irrelevant chunks into the top-5.\n",
    "- The **dynamic α router will show measurable MRR improvement** because weighting the correct engine for each query type cuts through the noise.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both pipelines use the **Asymmetric Security Filtering** from Phase 2 Step 4 (ChromaDB pre-filter + BM25 post-filter) to ensure zero breaches."
   ]
  },
